.TH F3N2WM 1 "September 2026" "f3n2wm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
f3n2wm \- A dynamic tiling window manager for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B f3n2wm
.SH DESCRIPTION
f3n2wm is a dynamic tiling window manager for Linux, written in LuaJIT with
direct X11 FFI bindings. It uses TOML for configuration and Lua for
extensibility.
.PP
Windows are automatically arranged as they open, close, or move. The window
manager supports multiple layouts, workspaces, keyboard-first navigation, and
a scriptable IPC interface for external control.
.SH CONFIGURATION
f3n2wm reads its configuration from TOML files:
.IP \(bu 3
/etc/f3n2wm/f3n2wm.toml (system config)
.IP \(bu 3
$HOME/.config/f3n2wm/f3n2wm.toml (user config)
.PP
User config is merged with system defaults, so only changed values need to be
specified. Press Mod4+r to reload the configuration without restarting.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
The default modifier key is Mod4 (Super/Windows key).
.PP
.nf
Mod4+Return        Open terminal
Mod4+d             Application launcher
Mod4+h/j/k/l       Focus left/down/up/right
Mod4+Space         Cycle layout
Mod4+1-0           Switch workspace
Mod4+q             Close window
Mod4+f             Fullscreen
Mod4+t             Toggle floating
Mod4+r             Reload config
Mod4+F2            Restart f3n2wm
Mod4+F3            Exit f3n2wm
.fi
.SH LAYOUTS
master-stack, spiral, monocle, grid, tabbed
.SH IPC
f3n2wm exposes a Unix socket for IPC at $HOME/.cache/f3n2wm-ipc.sock.
.SH FILES
.IP \(bu 3
$HOME/.config/f3n2wm/f3n2wm.toml
.IP \(bu 3
$HOME/.config/f3n2wm/layouts/
.IP \(bu 3
/etc/f3n2wm/f3n2wm.toml
